pared to leans, consumed more food under free-feeding conditions.", "reference": "2012, Obesity: New Insights for the Healthcare Professional, page 56:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": []}, {"language": {"code": "en", "name": "English"}, "partOfSpeech": "verb", "pronunciations": [{"type": "ipa", "text": "/ˈliːn/", "tags": []}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "[ˈlɪi̯n] ~ [ˈlɪ̈i̯n]", "tags": []}], "forms": [{"word": "leans", "tags": ["present", "singular", "third-person"]}, {"word": "leaning", "tags": ["participle", "present"]}, {"word": "leaned", "tags": ["participle", "past"]}, {"word": "leaned", "tags": ["past"]}], "senses": [{"definition": "To thin out (a fuel-air mixture): to reduce the fuel flow into the mixture so that there is more air or oxygen.", "tags": [], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "He leaned the mixture in an effort to cause a backfire through the carburetor, the generally accepted method of breaking the ice loose.", "reference": "1938 July, Harold Blaine Miller, Dupont Miller, “Weather Hop”, in Boys' Life, Boy Scouts of America, →ISSN, page 25:"}, {"text": "Even the Pilot's Operating Handbooks (POH) for our training airplanes add to our paranoia with their insistence that we not lean the mixture until we're above 5000 feet density altitude.", "reference": "2002 July, Tom Benenson, “Can Your Engine Run Too Lean?”, in Flying, volume 129, number 7, →ISSN, page 73:"}], "synonyms": ["derich", "disenrich"], "antonyms": ["enrich"], "translations": [{"language": {"code": "es", "name": "Spanish"}, "word": "enmagrecer"}], "subsenses": []}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": []}, {"language": {"code": "en", "name": "English"}, "partOfSpeech": "noun", "pronunciations": [{"type": "ipa", "text": "/ˈliːn/", "tags": []}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "[ˈlɪi̯n] ~ [ˈlɪ̈i̯n]", "tags": []}], "forms": [], "senses": [{"definition": "(US slang) A recreational drug composed of codeine-promethazine cough syrup mixed with usually soda and associated with the hip-hop culture of the Southern United States.", "tags": ["US", "slang", "uncountable"], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "Eyes real tight 'cause I'm chokin' the creep; vision messed up 'cause I'm drinkin' the lean.", "reference": "2005, “Stay Fly”, in Jordan Houston, Darnell Carlton, Paul Beauregard, Premro Smith, Marlon Goodwin, David Brown, Willie Hutchinson (lyrics), Most Known Unknown, performed by Three 6 Mafia (featuring Young Buck, 8 Ball, and MJG), Sony BMG:"}, {"text": "\"What's in the cup, let me see that / Girl, where the rest of that promethazine at?\" / She said, \"Cool, gotta run out to my Cadillac though / And I'll be like Fat Joe, and bring the lean back\"", "reference": "2020, “Those Kinda Nights”, in Music to Be Murdered By, performed by Eminem ft. Ed Sheeran:"}], "synonyms": ["blood", "mud", "purple drank", "sizzurp", "snot", "syrup"], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": []}], "source": {"url": "https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lean", "license": {"name": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/"}}}}